  "post": {
    "caption": "Everyday dust can scratch softer gems, because quartz in dust ranks 7 on the Mohs scale. Mineralogist Friedrich Mohs created the scale more than 200 years ago, ranking ten minerals from talc at 1 to diamond at 10. Each one scratches the minerals below it, the steps are uneven, and the jump to diamond is the biggest. Hardness isn't toughness, so a hard knock can still chip a diamond.",
